            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MsSuzyQ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "KFC's coleslaw is the only slaw I will eat, so I was so happy to find this recipe. But I did make a few changes - I cut the sugar down to 1/4 cup and left out the buttermilk (I don't like it, so I don't buy it!). I also used cider vinegar instead of white vinegar. I added some celery seed for a little extra flavor. My husband says it's the best he's ever had, so I have to beat him to the bowl if I want any!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carol Anne"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Absolutely delicious. Got rave reviews. Decreased sugar to 1/4 cup, used one package of shredded cabbage and carrots slaw mix, and added a dash or two of celery seed. Fabulous!",
            "datePublished": "2018-08-09T04:23:03.870Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lysa Riggs"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I tried to find a recipe with very little sugar as most Coleslaws are loaded with it. This recipe was appealing even though it still had too much sugar. I used 1/16 of a cup &amp; added 1tbsp horseradish for a kick. Could have added more. Next time, I’ll skip the milk, double the buttermilk &amp; probably cut the sugar again. Maybe add celery seed. I like tangy!",
            "datePublished": "2024-09-01T20:40:41.362Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "illusive"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This has become our one and only slaw for cook outs and when we are having smoked tenderloin... it is the perfect topper for BBQ pork sandwiches!\nI made a few personal changes... I don't use the regular milk only the butter milk. I have also increased the vinegar to 2 Tbs but I use half rice vinegar and half white wine vinegar. I also add approx 1/4 teas crushed tarragon to the vinegar. I normally use the bagged Angel hair shredded cabbage from the market . I prefer the finer shred and less of the extra thick core cuts of purple cabbage you find in prepackaged slaw mix.",
            "datePublished": "2016-07-15T22:59:03.390Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bob Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was able to find bags of finely chopped cabbage and put an entire 10 oz bag of carrots to 2 lbs of cabbage. Used apple cider vinegar because that's what I had and a little less lemon juice. And always Hellman's mayo. It was perfect and everyone raved and said it tasted like the original KFC and not what they serve now. It was a big hit with grilled pork chops and a definite keeper!!",
            "datePublished": "2015-09-27T20:36:08.217Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gunfighterzero"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the best coleslaw ever, even slaw haters love. I took a gallon of it to a work function and people raved about it. Letting it sit in the fridge overnight is a must for full flavor",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-23T23:06:28.306Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary Songer Willard Frye"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a last minute addition to dinner this evening. I made it and only \"soaked\" it for an hour. It was very delicious! I'm sure the remaining part will be even better tomorrow. It was easy and well worth the effort!",
            "datePublished": "2023-09-20T03:47:56.526Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tamontione"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe, because I am a sucker for creamy coleslaw with barbecue. I omitted the buttermilk, continue to mix the other ingredients together as directed. I added the coleslaw cabbage to the mixture, and then added 1/2 cup blue cheese dressing. It is amazing.",
            "datePublished": "2021-08-28T17:06:23.593Z"
