            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CHEFLORI"
            },
            "reviewBody": "LOVED IT ! Followed the recipe the 1st time and it was great. The 2nd time i omited regular milk, used apple cider vinegar instead of distilled vinegar and added a pinch of celery salt. The buttermilk is a must it makes the recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-25T05:33:46.513Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "backdoc"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I always follow the recipe closely, except I like onion, so I add about a half of a medium to small onion. I am very happy with the results. Everybody loves it and I always have to dig up the link to share it with them.\n\nIt's true what others have said, there's an excess of liquid. But, I think that's partly why it tastes so good. And, it's perfectly fine with me. It's not a problem. After marinating, you can strain it to remove the excess moisture.\n\nFinally, do make it well in advance of when you intend to serve it. I normally make it 12-24 hours early.",
            "datePublished": "2016-08-29T13:40:10.537Z"
          },
